   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands Red Cross</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Water the Heart of Climate Action in Sudan: Accelerating and scaling up water action to reduce risks and increase climate resilience</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Communities most at risk of climate change and water-related crises in River Nile, Sudan</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">River Nile State, Sudan</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sudan is exposed to several geophysical and climate-related hazards, some of which are increasing in frequency and magnitude. The country has seen unprecedented spikes in acute food insecurity, notably due to dry spells and erratic rains and socioeconomic variability, whilst simultaneously dealing with floods. Several vulnerability indices rank Sudan among the most vulnerable countries in the world to climate variability and change. There has been a great investment in integrated water resources management, with a focus on flood resilience specifically, however there is still a need for putting in place foundational policies and systems for flood risk management and safety protocols for water harvesting structures.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The current climate change and water crisis in Africa are inextricably linked together and require systemic changes. This project drives that change using an integrated climate and water approach to deal with increasing exposure to water related risks, bringing together different disciplines in the water, climate and disaster management sectors. It fosters  collaboration of global, national and local partners that traditionally have been working separately around the 5 broad technical focus areas specified above.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project addresses climate change and water related risks in Sudan around 5 main technical focus areas of &apos;Pillars&apos;:
1. Water-related risk knowledge and governance
2. Observations, monitoring and forecasting of weather and water-related hazards
3. Water specific early warning systems dissemination and communication
4. Anticipatory Action and Locally Led Adaptation and
5. Crosscutting activities</narrative>
  </description>
